# Secrets & local config
# Broad on purpose: `.env` alone does not match `.env.prod`, which is how a
# production secret file nearly got staged.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated data — regenerate with `make gen-data`
backend/data/corpus/
backend/data/eval/
backend/data/models/
# backend/data/demo/ (datagen's mixed-scenario demo log file) is generated output too, same as
# the three above — the special-case exception that used to live here existed only to keep
# DEMO_MODE's committed precomputed verdicts visible to a reviewer with no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# DEMO_MODE was removed entirely (docs/v2_migration change 12); nothing under this path is
# committed anymore.
backend/data/demo/
#
# backend/data/models/ IS ignored, and that is a real tradeoff rather than an oversight: the
# fitted artifacts total 171 MB, dominated by ecod.joblib at 125 MB and lof.joblib at 33 MB.
# Both models are instance-based — ECOD keeps the training matrix to evaluate its per-dimension
# ECDFs, LOF keeps it for neighbour lookups — so the artifact *is* the training set, and no
# serialization trick makes that small. GitHub hard-rejects a single file over 100 MB, so
# ecod.joblib could not be committed even if the tradeoff went the other way. `make train`
# rebuilds every artifact in ~165 s, deterministically, from a seeded corpus.
# NOT ignored: backend/evals/results.md. docs/12 calls it a deliverable referenced from
# the README — a reviewer has to be able to read the benchmark results without running
# anything. It is generated by `make eval`, but it ships.

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Runtime
*.log
# ...except the committed sample logs. `*.log` above exists for stray runtime output; these are
# a deliberate deliverable — the README tells a reviewer to upload one, so they have to be in the
# repo. Seeded and reproducible via `datagen` (backend/data/samples/README.md).
!backend/data/samples/*.log
frontend/next-env.d.ts
